                <pb facs="0246" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/73.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The minister for foreign affairs has requested me to inform you that a
                    communication goes forward by to-day’s mail instructing the Dominican
                    plenipotentiaries to endeavor by every possible effort to effect a satisfactory
                    settlement of the boundary dispute and not to break off negotiations before
                    consulting with the Secretary of State of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
